Vendored UI icons — Lucide (https://lucide.dev, https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide)

These SVGs are copied unmodified from the Lucide icon set and bundled here so the
plugin ships fully offline (no CDN, no npm/build step — the plugin has no runtime
dependency on anything outside NetBox itself). Lucide is ISC-licensed; some glyphs
derive from Feather (MIT). The full upstream license text is vendored alongside as
./LICENSE.

The frontend does NOT load these files at runtime. Their path bodies are inlined
verbatim — into the `Icons` static class (static/netbox_facilitymap/lib.js), for UI
chrome, AND into `DeviceShapes` (static/netbox_facilitymap/device-shapes.js + its
server-side mirror device_shapes.py), for the schematic device markers whose role
maps cleanly to a Lucide glyph. Each returns the glyph on Lucide's native 24×24
viewBox. These files are the auditable source of truth for those inlined paths —
regenerate the consumer after replacing an icon here.

